# Key material must never enter this repository.
#
# git-bootstrap reads the keypair from --keys-dir, so the keys belong on the
# removable volume, not in a clone. These patterns are the second line of
# defence for the case where one gets copied in here by mistake — the repo is
# public, so a single careless `git add -A` would publish a private key.

git@github.com
git@github.com.pub

# Anything else key-shaped, in case the naming convention ever changes.
id_*
*.pub
*.key
*.pem

# Secret files, the shape every repository here ignores (CLAUDE-practices §2).
# Nothing in git-bootstrap reads one; this is the same second line of defence.
*.secret
*.secrets
secrets/

# Encrypted key bundles.
*.gpg
*.asc
keys.tar*

# Editor swap files: these hold file contents, including whatever was open.
.*.sw?
*~
